{"id":"NCT06846281","title":"Efficacy and Safety of Remibrutinib After Switching From Ocrelizumab in Participants Living With Relapsing Multiple Sclerosis.","official":"A Randomized, Open-label, Parallel-group, Non-inferiority Study Comparing Efficacy, Safety, and Tolerability of Remibrutinib After Switching From Ocrelizumab in Participants Living With Relapsing Multiple Sclerosis, Followed by Open-label Treatment With Remibrutinib","summary":"The purpose of this Phase 3b study is to assess the efficacy, safety and tolerability of remibrutinib after switching from ocrelizumab and compared to continuous ocrelizumab treatment, in patients living with relapsing multiple sclerosis (plwRMS).","conditions":["Relapsing Multiple Sclerosis"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"Remibrutinib oral treatment"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Ocrelizumab"}],"criteria":"Key Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Male or female aged 40 to 70 years (inclusive)\n* Diagnosis of RMS according to the 2017 McDonald diagnostic criteria\n* Treated with ocrelizumab according to routine clinical practice and at standard dose\n* Neurologically stable within 30 days\n* Suitable to be switched to remibrutinib based on physician judgement or patient preference\n\nKey Exclusion Criteria:\n\n* Diagnosis of primary progressive multiple sclerosis (PPMS) according to the revised 2017 McDonald criteria\n* History of clinically significant Central Nervous System disease or neurological disorders\n* History of confirmed Progressive Multifocal Leukoencephalopathy or neurological symptoms consistent\n* Active clinically significant systemic bacterial, viral, parasitic or fungal infections\n* Active, chronic disease of the immune system other than MS\n* Severe cardiac disease or significant findings on the ECG\n* Participant who is unable to undergo MRI scans\n* History of life-threatening infusion or injection reaction related to ocrelizumab\n* Participants not adequately controlled on ocrelizumab (CD19+ B-cell count ≥10 cells/µL at screening)\n\nOther inclusion and exclusion criteria may apply","minAge":"40 Years","maxAge":"70 Years","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":400,"start":"2025-06-23","pcd":"2029-07-25","upd":"2026-10-26","sponsor":"Novartis Pharmaceuticals","areas":["neurology"],"central":["Novartis Pharmaceuticals · 1-888-669-6682 · novartis.email@novartis.com","Novartis Pharmaceuticals · +41613241111"],"sites":[{"f":"Perseverance Research Center","city":"Scottsdale","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85253","s":"R","lat":33.5092,"lon":-111.899,"c":"Adriana Romero · aromero@prcresearcheducation.com"},{"f":"University of California Irvine","city":"Irvine","pr":"California","zip":"92697","s":"R","lat":33.6695,"lon":-117.8231,"c":"Veronica Martin · vero@hs.uci.edu"},{"f":"Medstar Washington Hospital Center","city":"Washington D.C.","pr":"District of Columbia","zip":"20010-2975","s":"R","lat":38.8951,"lon":-77.0364,"c":"Anu Bhooshan · +1 202 877 8946 · anu.r.bhooshan@medstar.net"},{"f":"Neurology of Central FL Res Ctr","city":"Altamonte Springs","pr":"Florida","zip":"32714","s":"R","lat":28.6611,"lon":-81.3656,"c":"Adiana Perez · +1 407 790 4990 · adiresearchcfl@gmail.com"},{"f":"University of Florida","city":"Gainesville","pr":"Florida","zip":"32610","s":"R","lat":29.6516,"lon":-82.3248,"c":"Whitney Miller · wjm1433@ufl.edu"},{"f":"Memorial Healthcare System","city":"Hollywood","pr":"Florida","zip":"33021","s":"R","lat":26.0112,"lon":-80.1495,"c":"Hina Khan · +1 954 265 6934 · hikhan@mhs.net"},{"f":"Neurology Associates PA","city":"Maitland","pr":"Florida","zip":"32751","s":"R","lat":28.6278,"lon":-81.3631,"c":"Nicole Perovic · +1 407 647 5996 · nicole.naparesearch@gmail.com"},{"f":"Elite Clinical Research","city":"Miami","pr":"Florida","zip":"33144","s":"R","lat":25.7743,"lon":-80.1937,"c":"Rebeca Fernandez · +1 305 262 3396 · rfernandez@eliteclinicalresearch.com"},{"f":"Aqualane Clinical Research","city":"Naples","pr":"Florida","zi